Tom asked for some advice about playing V:

<snipped>

>Weapons - +6 Excalibur (was my starting longsword, and I want to ascend
>with it.)  Mojo and Grayswandir unenchanted.

IIRC, Mojo is not as good against As because they are shock resistant, and that
is Mojo's attack.  You might want to enchant up a vanilla silver sabre to use
to two-weapon later (good with Greyswandir against demons and later for use
with Excalibur)

<snipped>

>I have yet to find GoPower,
>and I don't have any good way to deal with mind flayers or curses yet.
>I'm not particularly attached to the conducts, though it'd be nice to
>finish with at least a couple of them.  My main concern is with mind
>flayers -- how should I deal with them?
>
>Here are some of the options I've thought of:
>- break wishless conduct to get GoP, and use the Mojo Yoyo to take out
>mind flayers

Not a bad option, especially if you don't find the GoP soon.

>- reverse geno silver dragons for scales, chug a couple !oGEnergy and get
>rid of the shield, so I can cast magic missile reliably and effectively

I have never had much luck casting spells with a V.  Besides, later you would
have to remove your GoP to cast effectively, and that takes time.  It might be
worth a try though, if you don't find more wands.

>- go kill a priest for a robe, and polypile for an "oReflection so I can
>get rid of the shield and cast magic missile...

That might improve your odds at spell-casting, but sounds like a short-term
solution.

<snipped>

>- Enchant a stack of daggers, and use them to soften up the mind flayers
>at range
>

A very good idea.

<snipped>

>
>What are some other options?  What should I do to give this character good
>chances of surviving?

Grease your helmet.

>Is it worth trying to keep conducts, or should I
>just geno at will?  I'm not used to playing anything that can't just magic
>missile everything that comes its way.

Valks are pretty kick-ass fighters.  You just need to rethink your strategy,
count on wands more often, and start practicing two-weaponing.

Conducts are a matter of choice.  It depends how much you want the extra
challenge.

Good luck!

